 ("R-214",2,"Audio","Game volume boost","P2","done","S","BBRR Settings > Game Volume 100-200%; loud passages rounded off by a limiter instead of distorting; a log line reports how loud the game mix is","R-201","Requested 2026-11-12: the game is quieter than other programs at full volume. The SDK already had an output gain (rex/audio/downmix.h) that nothing set; it hard-clipped above full scale. SDK patch 0018 applies a gain above 1 after the channel mix with a soft limiter (knee at 0.8) and logs every 30 s the game mix peak and average level and how much was rounded off. Setting --game_volume, default 100%. Built, not run; the level line will show how much headroom the game leaves. Measured 2026-11-12 at 100% (Denon AVR, 6 channels): during songs the game mix peaks at -2 to 0 dBFS (bursts) but averages only -27 to -34 dBFS across the six channels (about -22 to -29 dBFS on the two front channels that carry the music), roughly 10 dB below typical PC audio. A wide-dynamic-range mix: a plain boost reaches the limiter on loud bursts. Suggested: try 150%-175% and watch the 'rounded off' share in the log; a compressor (lifting the quiet parts) would be the better long-term fix. Tested at 150% 2026-11-12: output peaks reach full scale only on bursts and 0.002-0.014% of samples were rounded off (inaudible); room to go higher. Settled 2026-11-12: no menu setting; the game plays at 150% by default (--game_volume to change it). Done."),

