 ("R-304",3,"Timing","Frame pacing matched to the display","P0","done","M","No frame-rate setting needed: the game runs at the display's refresh rate with each frame started on a real display refresh; no judder; optional unlimited mode","R-302","Untested: guest refresh rate = main display refresh (src/settings.cpp ApplyFrameRate); SDK patch 0002 ticks the guest vblank from the desktop compositor (DwmFlush) with an evenly spaced timer fallback and no millisecond sleeps in the GPU wait. Before: 120 fps limit gave 5.5-12 ms frame times (judder) on a 120 Hz display Tracker clean-up 2026-11-12: marked done. The log of 2026-11-12 shows steady pacing on the user's 120 Hz display: frame time average 8.33 ms, 7.75-8.94 ms, 0 late frames over 10 s stretches. The optional unlimited mode was not built."),
