 ("R-415",4,"UI","Ultrawide menu/HUD layout pass","P1","todo","M","During the full playtest, every menu and HUD screen is checked at 21:9 and 32:9 with both Menu Layout options (Screen Edges and Centred): side elements follow the window edges, nothing splits from its group or pops during animations; fixes via grouping rules or per-screen overrides (--ui_anchor_debug log)","R-402,R-110","2026-11-11: menus were drawn in their 16:9 place for a moment after a transition and then jumped to the edge; the finished layout of each screen is remembered (cache/ui_layout.txt) and used for the first 1.5 s after a screen loads. First attempt failed (it learned an in-between arrangement the main menu holds for ~0.3 s); second attempt only learns what is still there after 1.5 s; third also places items that are spread out while arriving (flying text). Confirmed fixed in play 2026-11-11. Standing rule from the user: test menu changes with both Menu Layout options. Song-select headings and speed panel are kept with the list instead of following the edges. Edge anchoring works on most menus but not all (user test 2026-11-10); do with the full playtest 2026-11-11 (2): pause menu snapped late on its first visit (nothing learned yet); hit timing numbers jumped to the window edges when the arrow was in the outer third; results screen split apart (labels and Rating sent to the edges). Fixes, untested: finished layouts now ship in ui_scripts/ui_layout.txt (30 screens from the user's cache) so first visits are right; HUD readout band and results area kept centred via bbrr.ui.keep. 2026-11-11 (3): pause menu items lost their edge place while a dialogue (End Song?) was open over it; while a Popups script is up, the covered screen now keeps its finished layout. Untested."),
