 ("R-414",4,"UI","In-game Revolution settings menu","P0","done","L","'BBRR Settings' entry in the game's own Help & Options menu opens a settings screen in the game's style (spinner rows, A save / B cancel / X defaults); settings saved to a file and applied at start-up; home for the calibration screen","R-401","First version (untested): UI scripts are Lua 5.1 and can be replaced from ui_scripts/ (src/ui_mod.cpp); screen ui_scripts/Options/BBRR.lua with aspect ratio, menu layout, audio offset, skip intro; saved to settings.ini (src/settings.cpp). Still to add: resolution scale, frame rate, window mode, DLC, calibration Tracker clean-up 2026-11-12: marked done. The menu has been in daily use for days: pages Profiles, Video Settings, Calibration, Modifiers, Keyboard (see docs/USER_GUIDE.md); the note above describes the first version only."),
 ("R-417",4,"Lighting","Fireworks reflected in the water","P2","in_progress","M","Bursts and sparks show in the water's reflection, optional","R-410","Researched 2026-11-12 (docs/GRAPHICS.md, Water reflections): the water samples a mirror pass of the sky, city and ground-level lights; the sparks and smoke are only drawn in the normal pass. Options: firework light on the water via the water shader's light constants (small), or drawing the sparks again in the mirror pass from the game side (medium, needs a probe build first). 2026-11-12: both built as Video Settings toggles, not run. Correction to the research: the 4,000-point draw 63B4/4B1E is not the sparks (its pixel shader multiplies by c11.x = 0, so it draws nothing: likely a star field switched off); the bursts are BA59/7C30 (up to ~19,000 points), the lit smoke BBFF/9567, and rockets with their trails 1DB9/C471 are already in the mirror pass. Water Glow (--water_glow): the water's single specular highlight (light position c2, shininess c3, colour c4; the moon) is moved to this frame's fireworks and given their colour, shininess 20. Water Reflections (--water_reflections): the burst draw is issued a second time with the mirror camera captured from the city's mirror pass (C837 c0-c3); whether it shows depends on whether the water writes depth - the first frame logs the depth state of the water and burst draws ('[bbrr] water draw: depth test ...'). SDK patch 0019. Test 2026-11-12: Water Glow looked really nice and is to be kept (now on by default at Medium) - but only the rocket tails showed in the water, and the user wants the light that falls on the buildings to fall on the water too. Patch 0020: the highlight spreads wider (shininess 6 instead of 20; Video Settings > Water Glow Spread: Narrow 20 / Medium 6 / Wide 2) and the fireworks' colour washes over the water (ambient green and blue, --water_glow_wash 0.06; red is left alone as it also sets the water's opacity). Water Glow has levels Off / Low / Medium / High. Water Reflections: the log shows the burst draw has no depth test (and the water writes depth), so the mirrored copy painted over everything - seen in visualizer mode. Doing it properly means drawing the bursts into the mirror picture before the water reads it (a register-state snapshot replayed in the next frame's mirror pass); kept as 'Water Reflections (test)', off by default. Settled 2026-11-12: the Spread row is gone, the highlight is always Narrow (shininess 20; --water_glow_spread still works); Water Glow Off / Low / Medium / High with High the default."),

 ("R-501",5,"Achievements","Local achievements from SPA","P1","done","M","12 achievements (200G) tracked and toasted; persisted","R-107","ReXGlue has an achievements XEX-to-TOML extractor 2026-11-12: the SDK already unlocks from the SPA, saves progress and shows a toast; F7 lists them. Built, untested: SDK patch 0006 implements XamShowAchievementsUI(Ex) (was a stub, so the in-game Achievements menu did nothing) as a XAM dialog with the same list and icons, closed with B / A / Back / Esc, scrolled with d-pad or left stick. Seen working 2026-11-12; list made opaque over a darkened screen. Overlays in HDR: patch 0006 also gives the immediate drawer an HDR pixel shader (sRGB made linear, scaled to the paper white), so ImGui menus are no longer dim with HDR on; untested. HDR overlays confirmed good 2026-11-12. In-game list shows the achievements of the player who opened it (XamShowAchievementsUI user index). Confirmed 2026-11-12."),
 ("R-502",5,"Leaderboards","Local leaderboards","P0","in_progress","M","66 scoreboard IDs (contents.txt) store top scores locally per mode/difficulty","R-107","Verified 2026-11-10: scores show in song select and persist across restarts (src/leaderboards.cpp) Correction 2026-11-12: this was never working. The log shows the local score table has always been empty ('loaded 0 views', no score ever written): the game only writes leaderboard scores through an Xbox Live session, which a local profile never starts. The scores seen on song select on 2026-11-10 come from the game's own save data, not from this table. 2026-11-12 (evening): working with the Leaderboards Test setting on (SDK patch 0017, profiles reported as signed in to Xbox Live): a song's score was saved locally (views 1, 47, 249 in leaderboards.txt), shown on the game's own leaderboard screen, and the game's leaderboard view appeared after the song. To do: decide whether the setting becomes the default, and watch for side effects of the game believing it is online."),
 ("R-503",5,"Leaderboards","Implement XUserReadStats / XSessionWriteStats / stats enumerator","P0","in_progress","L","Game's own leaderboard screens show data; XamUserCreateStatsEnumerator implemented","R-502","ReadStats path verified via song select; full leaderboard screens (ByRank/ByXuid enumerators) still to verify 2026-11-12: the user reports the main menu's Leaderboards entry has always been greyed out, so the screens were never reachable. Cause: the menu script switches the entry off unless the profile is signed in to Xbox Live (local profiles report signed in locally). ui_scripts/Main/MainMenu.lua now keeps the entry on, and logs the call ('[ui] main menu SetItemActive'). Built, not run; what the screens behind it do (they start an Xbox Live session) is unknown. 2026-11-12 first test: the entry is selectable now, but choosing it showed the game's 'not signed in' message (the menu checks Profile.HasOnlineProfile again when the entry is chosen). ui_scripts/Main/MainMenu.lua and new wrappers for LbChooseGameType, LbChooseSong and Leaderboards now run those screens as if signed in. Not run. Later 2026-11-12: the menu check is in the main menu's Message function (found by disassembling the compiled Lua; a small Lua 5.1 bytecode lister was written for this); with Message run as if signed in, the user reached the leaderboard screens. The table then said the player was offline: the reader's start step (sub_8209A1E0) wants sign-in state 2 (Xbox Live) in the game's player record (0x821D4180 + 64 x player, +56) and local profiles are 1. A hook now shows 2 for the length of that call only. Song lengths and tempos are no longer drawn on the leaderboard screens' song list (requested). Built, not run. 2026-11-12 (later): with the sign-in fix the table opens but every board says no scores - because nothing has ever been written (see R-502). The write path (sub_82079DC0 -> sub_820C2EF8 / sub_820C3098 -> XSessionWriteStats) needs a session object, a stats object and a started session, none of which exist offline. Experiment, built, not run: SDK patch 0017 and a restart-only setting 'Leaderboards Test' report local profiles as signed in to Xbox Live so the game runs its own session and stats code against the SDK's local stand-ins. 2026-11-12 (evening): the game's leaderboard screens show the saved scores (user-confirmed with the Leaderboards Test setting on). A second profile as Player 2 saw Player 1's score, as expected for a table shared by everyone on this PC."),
 ("R-504",9,"Online","Online leaderboard service","P1","todo","XL","Self-hosted REST service; scores submitted & fetched; basic validation","R-503"," Moved to the post-1.0 stretch goals 2026-11-12 at the user's request."),
