 ("R-506",5,"Online","Player identity / profile","P1","done","S","Local gamertag; optional online account token","R-504"," 2026-11-12, built, untested: SDK patch 0006 adds the user_gamertag setting (UserProfile::name(), max 15 characters, User if empty) and an exported text box (rex::kernel::xam::ShowTextEntryDialog); BBRR Settings has a Gamertag row (action:gamertag, current name in STR117) that opens it; saved in settings.ini. Second local profile not done (R-604). The name in the game's corner did not change at first: the game reads names only on a notification, so a new name now sends XN_SYS_PROFILESETTINGCHANGED (0x0E), which its handler (sub_820C5650) answers by reading every name again; untested. 2026-11-12: replaced by real local profiles (see R-604): the single-name gamertag setting moved each name to its own save folder, so renaming lost the progress. Done through local profiles (R-604)."),

 ("R-601",6,"Input","Controller support (XInput, DualSense, Switch Pro)","P0","done","S","All controllers work via SDL3 with hot-plug","R-104"," Tracker clean-up 2026-11-12: marked done for now at the user's decision. Xbox controllers work, with a choice of which pad is Player 1 and two players tested; PlayStation and Switch controllers are untested and precise input is XInput-only."),
 ("R-602",6,"Input","Keyboard support & rebinding","P0","done","M","Default 4-colour + D-pad mapping; full rebinding UI","R-601"," 2026-11-12, built, untested: the SDK already emulates a pad from the keyboard (--mnk_mode, keybind_* cvars). The port turns it on by default (BBRR Settings > Keyboard) with its own keys: W A S D face buttons in pad positions, arrows d-pad, Enter = A too, Backspace = B too, Esc = Start, Tab = Back, Q / E = LB / RB, Space = both triggers, sticks unbound; saved in settings.ini. Rebinding page: next. Default keys and Q/E speed steps confirmed 2026-11-12 (LB/RB now read from the game's own controller read, NoteGuestButtons, so the keyboard and SDL pads count). Then, untested: Keyboard page (src/keyboard.cpp): Use Keyboard, D-pad (arrows / numpad / IJKL), one row per button showing its keys (STR92-99), A then a key rebinds (key taken off other buttons, Esc cancels, guest input held meanwhile), Reset Keys. Keyboard page confirmed 2026-11-12; Use Keyboard now only changes when the page is saved (switching it at once locked the keyboard out, and adding the keyboard device made a held pad press count twice)."),
 ("R-603",6,"Input","Button glyph swap","P2","todo","M","UI shows Xbox/PlayStation/keyboard prompts to match device","R-602",""),
 ("R-604",6,"Input","Local 2-player","P1","done","S","Two controllers, or controller + keyboard","R-601"," 2026-11-12, built, untested: local profiles. SDK patch 0006: KernelState::SignInUser / SignOutUser / user_profile(slot) for slots 0-3, XamUser* calls answer for any signed-in slot, profile title data kept by XUID (content/<title>/profile/<XUID>, the old name folder is moved over), achievements per profile (achievements/<XUID>/<title>.toml; slot from the XGI entry's first word; other slots written without a pop-up). Game: src/profiles.cpp keeps profiles.ini (up to 8; original XUID B13EBABEBABEBABE named User keeps the old data), BBRR Settings > Profiles picks Player 1 / Player 2 (None), renames and creates; saving signs them in and sends XN_SYS_SIGNINCHANGED (0x0A), a rename sends 0x0E. Assumption to check: multiplayer works with any second controller; Player 2 profile only adds a name, save data and achievements for it. Pop-up profile picker: later if needed. 2026-11-12: seen working (two profiles, two controllers; old scores kept under User; per-player achievements list). Profiles page: Left/Right pick Player 1 / Player 2 and skip the other player's profile; A saves; rename rows show no name. Controllers: SDL connection order = player order (first found is Player 1). Open: Swap Controllers row or press-to-join, delete profile, launcher field. 2026-11-12, built, untested: Player 1 Controller row (SDK patch 0007: SlotAssignment preferred order by device key <guid>#<n>, InputSystem::ListControllers / SetPlayerOrder, XN_SYS_INPUTDEVICESCHANGED sent); saved as player1_controller in profiles.ini. Player 1 Controller confirmed working 2026-11-12. Tracker clean-up 2026-11-12: marked done; the user tested two players during the controller and profile testing."),
 ("R-605",6,"UX","Settings persistence","P0","done","S","User TOML in %APPDATA%; CLI overrides","R-414"," Tracker clean-up 2026-11-12: marked done. Settings are saved to <Documents>/boomboomrocket/settings.ini (one 'cvar = value' per line, not TOML in %APPDATA% as first written) and command-line options win over them."),
